{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQ2zJPtrQTkqyziZHV2d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't calculate the take rate for FY2022, FY2023 or FY2024 because I couldn't find Airbnb's Gross Booking Value in these tools. I found revenue (the top half of the ratio) but not the bottom half, so I can't comment on the trend either.\n\n**What I found (annual revenue from Airbnb's 10-K filings):**\n- FY2022: $8,399 million\n- FY2023: $9,917 million\n- FY2024: $11,102 million\n\n**What's missing:**\n- **Not in the structured data.** Gross Booking Value isn't a standard reported data item, and the data tool returned nothing beyond standard revenue figures.\n- **Not in the filing text I could reach.** A full-text search confirmed that each of the three 10-Ks below uses the term \"Gross Booking Value,\" but the search only lists matching filings, not the text or figures in them.\n- **My guesses weren't confirmed.** I searched for three exact phrases stating Gross Booking Value amounts I recalled ($81.8B, $73.3B, $63.2B). All three returned no matches, so I haven't used those numbers.\n\n**To finish this:** get Gross Booking Value for each year from the \"Key Business Metrics\" section of the 10-Ks below. Then divide revenue by Gross Booking Value for each year to get the take rate.\n\n**Sources**\n- 10-K for FY2022, filed 2023-02-17, accession 0001559720-23-000003\n- 10-K for FY2023, filed 2024-02-16, accession 0001559720-24-000006\n- 10-K for FY2024, filed 2025-02-13, accession 0001559720-25-000010"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1040,"cache_read_input_tokens":8244,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1040},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":nul